sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Staff as Staff/Admin
  participant Guard as JWT/Role guard
  participant API as SettlementService
  participant Idem as IdempotencyService
  participant Port as US14 SaleActivation
  participant Review as US21 PaymentReview
  participant DB as MongoDB replica set
  participant Events as NotificationsService
  Staff->>Guard: POST /transactions/:id/confirm-payment + UUID key + actual receipt evidence
  Guard->>API: Current authenticated actor + validated DTO
  API->>Idem: PAYMENT_CONFIRM, normalized input, targetId
  Idem->>DB: Start snapshot/majority transaction; read own operation key
  alt Same committed key/payload
    Idem-->>Staff: Original 200 SettlementResult
  else Different payload/target for same key
    Idem-->>Staff: 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT
  else New intent
    Idem->>API: work(session), callback may retry
    API->>DB: Read transaction/sale to identify lock targets
    API->>Port: activateSaleWithinSession(session, target, prepareSettlement)
    Port->>DB: Write member.service_revision then transaction.guard_revision
    Port->>DB: Reread PENDING transaction
    Port->>API: prepareSettlement after locks, same session
    API->>Review: Recheck state, snapshot, amount, account, time, reference
    Review->>DB: Read current eligibility and reference (simple collation)
    Review-->>API: Current canConfirm/blockingCodes
    API->>DB: Insert payment SUCCEEDED, invoice from locked buyer snapshot
    Note over API,DB: Unique reference and partial unique SUCCEEDED are final constraints
    API-->>Port: Preparation complete
    Port->>DB: Validate successful full payment, activate membership and actual sale dates
    Port-->>API: membershipId, startDate, endDate
    API->>DB: CAS PENDING/version to SETTLED/version+1
    API->>Events: Persist SERVICE_SALE_SETTLED + recipient snapshot (same session)
    Events->>DB: Notification + recipients + outbox
    API-->>Idem: Allowlisted SettlementResult and IDs
    Idem->>DB: Insert operation result; commit all
    Note over API,DB: Any error rolls back payment/invoice/membership/sale dates/event/operation
    Idem-->>Staff: 200 or structured error; unknown commit returns 503 and retains key
  end
  Staff->>Guard: GET /operations/PAYMENT_CONFIRM/:key after lost response
  Guard->>Idem: Current actor/permission
  Idem->>DB: Read own committed result
  Idem-->>Staff: Original result or 404 (may still be running)
  Note over Staff,DB: Retry uses the same key/input. Preview never reserves reference. CASH time is server; TRANSFER paid_at is verified receivedAt.
